 ## Overview
-Procedural instancing for voxel blocks replaces baked mesh geometry with a compact instance record per voxel, resolving position, color, and occlusion in the vertex shader using a shared cube template [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, unofficial]. It differs from standard hardware instancing by computing per-instance transformations and visibility flags (such as face culling) dynamically within the vertex shader, allowing for custom setup logic without CPU-side mesh generation [S3, S4, unofficial]. This method significantly reduces memory usage compared to baked geometries but increases vertex workload for dense layouts because it submits whole cubes and discards hidden faces in the shader [S1, S5, unofficial].
